the scp foundation has encountered its  fair share of incredibly tough  adversaries and fearsome monsters but  none are as formidable or at least as  durable as  scp-682 the hard to destroy reptile  we've talked about this behemoth before  in a number of mind-boggling videos and  all of the increasingly desperate  lengths the foundation has gone to in  order to terminate it we've gotten so  desperate to put this thing to a rest  that we've even reached out to all of  you for suggestions on the matter sadly  they've thrown 682 together with some of  the most destructive anomalies in  foundation custody and it's slithered  out of seemingly inescapable danger  every time so much so that we've noticed  certain researchers on the 682 case have  started drinking a little more heavily  as of late sometimes the threats didn't  leave so much as a dent in the monster's  scales sometimes the other creatures ran  screaming at the sight of it and  sometimes 682 mutated and twisted its  form in ways that were shocking even to  a foundation research team that's seen  just about all there is to see  after all 682's truly insane  adaptability has always been its number  one power and the key to its infuriating  death-defying abilities and these are  some of  scp-682's craziest mutations during one  round of tests  scp-682 was released into an enclosure  with scp-272  a nail that traps any living thing in  place when it is dropped onto the  organism's shadow 682 was surrounded by  32 000 watts stadium lights one of which  was switched on as soon as it entered  the enclosure a d-class dropped the nail  onto the creature's shadow it was  promptly pinned in place and all 30  lights were switched on and off in  random patterns causing the reptile to  be hurled around the room at devastating  speeds after nearly an hour of this  about 95 of the monster skin had been  worn down 63 of its teeth had been  broken from its jaw and its eyeballs had  come loose from their sockets at this  point something truly bizarre happened  the exposed tissue beneath 682's top  layer of skin previously bloody and dark  red began to give off a bright white  light the subdermal tissue grew steadily  brighter and brighter until it eclipsed  the glow from the stadium lights and  removed any shadows cast along the floor  it collapsed on the ground and continued  giving off violently bright light for  the next 48 hours so bright that it  caused permanent retinal damage to all  personnel in the room hell of a light  show but this next mutation proves just  how hard it is to lick as cp 682  especially when it develops the tools to  start licking back  scp-743 is a chocolate fountain that  exhibits some carnivorous qualities when  it is near a living organism especially  if it consumes the fountain's delicious  chocolate it produces swarms of ant-like  monsters that devour the organism piece  by piece carrying the bits into the  fountain until nothing is left the  research team was curious about the  possibilities of introducing 743 to 682  so it was transported to the reptile's  testing chamber within a few minutes  chocolate began to flow from the  fountain 682 was curious and began to  drink from it it may hate almost  everything but even 682 can't resist  chocolate it drank greedily for several  minutes until the foundation began  releasing the ants within moments 682  was covered in ants and in spite of its  best efforts to fight off the swarm it  was completely covered and rendered  immobile the ants made quick work of the  massive creature and after several  minutes it was stripped down to less  than 80 percent of its original mass it  seemed as if this might truly be it for  the beast but then it opened its mouth  it unfurled its tongue now over five  meters long and sticky comparable to an  enlarged version of an anteater's tongue  it began lapping up the ants thousands  at a time picked up by its mutated  tongue as it devoured the ants more  poured out of the fountain slicing off  pieces of 682's flesh with their  pinchers and carrying them back to the  fountain they reached a symbiotic pace  feeding on each other in equal measure  for hours until testing was terminated  that was a sticky situation but trust me  this next crazy mutation will really  blow you away  scp-3108 also known as the nerfing gun  is an altered toy gun that turns  anything it hits into an inferior  version of itself when the gun was fired  at a tissue sample taken from scp-682  the sample turned into a piece of tissue  from a giant leaf-tailed gecko hoping to  carry this over and turn 682 into a  harmless animal a d-class officer was  sent into the containment chamber to  fire the gun at the entity once it was  hit with the foam dart it began to  transform  unfortunately instead of becoming a  simple gecko it began to mutate it grew  larger its muscles bulging noticeably  beneath its scaly skin its teeth grew  longer sharper its tongue sprouting  teeth of its own it opened its mouth to  roar and it appeared that the teeth long  curved fangs with a deadly tip went all  the way back down the beast's throat  security officers were deployed to  temporarily neutralize the monster but  found that it was even more powerful  than before not only was it bigger but  it had developed a new ability when  threatened it would begin to vibrate at  a high rate grinding its teeth together  and would explode in a burst of fire and  meaty chunks fangs flew in every  direction like shrapnel tearing into  personnel and lodging in their skin this  is an impressive move but it seems like  a one-time trick right wrong the bits  and pieces no matter how tiny or how  flattened to mush would crawl back  together and form the creature all over  again it was able to escape containment  like this killing an untold number of  personnel before it was temporarily  incapacitated and returned to its  containment mutating back into life from  a self-induced explosion is pretty crazy  but surely you can't mutate back from  nothing at all right  right  oh boy i don't like that look you're  giving me  scp-3930 is a void located near yusink  russia within which nothing exists once  something has passed within its border  it ceases to be though outside observers  will be able to perceive them for a  small time after  scp-682 was brought into 3930 and it  walked inside once there it ceased  existing however even though 682 no  longer existed foundation personnel  looking at the void could still see the  beast whenever they viewed it a strong  image appeared in the brain of the  person looking and it had the exact  appearance of scp-682  somehow even when it didn't exist 682  was able to attack and kill various  personnel these people did not die from  physical damage but from their brain  function suddenly inexplicably stopping  the reptile defied the rules of the void  somehow causing real destruction even  though it was not real 15 hours later  682 was found in its containment chamber  as if nothing had happened at all it had  been snuffed out of existence and had  mutated its way back into reality with  no explanation well that was  existentially terrifying thank 343 at  least there's only one of those things  oh no  scp-3207 is a highly efficient mobile  war machine outfitted with cannons  capable of firing blasts that can  vaporize organic matter on contact this  seems like a good match for something  supposedly indestructible  3207 was fired at scp-682 several times  appearing to destroy it completely  except for a smudge on the floor of the  chamber the reptile was gone for a  duration of six hours before something  strange began to happen lobster tissue  began to clump together forming five  separate piles they pulled closer and  closer together compressing into five  reptilian creatures they writhed around  getting used to their new legs and teeth  snapping their jaws at any living thing  in sight overwhelming and surprising the  security personnel who had been lulled  into a false sense of security by the  apparent defeat of 682 the five smaller  versions of the entity were able to  escape containment once they had made it  into the hallway  they began to clamber over each other  their scales shifting eyeballs squeezing  together and fusing into one eye skin  stretching like hot rubber over  unnaturally bendy bone as the shocked  security personnel watched the five  lizards melted into one becoming a  full-sized version of scp-682  that was good as new they were able to  contain it after a great deal of effort  but one of the researchers requested a  note to be added to the research notes  for the day and applied going forward do  not explode okay so the big lizard is a  constant threat got it still wouldn't it  be nice if 682 could make itself a  little smaller i can't imagine anything  bad coming from that  scp-1056 is an anomalous kitchen timer  capable of changing the size of living  objects the foundation wanted to see how  long it would take 682 to return to its  original size after being shrunk so they  built a testing chamber connected to  1056's dial and released 682 inside  sealing the door behind it the dial was  set to 0.25 and the activation button  was pressed 682 thrashed around  bellowing as parts of its body expanded  and contracted at random then with no  warning it disappeared d-class personnel  were deployed to investigate the chamber  but it seemed to be completely gone  there was no sign of it it's pretty hard  to lose a giant lizard so naturally they  were all a bit perplexed the chamber was  kept sealed under the assumption that  682 had to still be inside somewhere  sometime later a security officer  spotted 682 outside of site 19 returned  to its original size somehow during the  test 682 used the effects of 1056 to  strengthen its ability to change its own  size it adapted and shrank to a size so  small that no one watching could even  see it anymore and it slipped out  through the sealed door it was even  temporarily able to change the size of  other objects around it shrinking  weapons used to contain down until they  were useless okay so 682 is pretty cool  under pressure but what if we made it a  whole lot colder most of the testing on  682 is done with other anomalies however  sometimes the foundation likes to  simplify it a bit dr carlson suggested  they try something a bit more basic  liquid nitrogen one ton of liquid  nitrogen was poured onto scp-682 from  above as it tends to do the liquid  nitrogen promptly froze the bees solid  they remain stuck in place for about 10  minutes until it began to melt the  frozen cast around it its core body  temperature seemed to skyrocket  producing intense heat that fully thawed  it in three minutes it didn't stop there  though the temperature continued to  increase growing hotter and hotter as if  to deliberately punish the research  staff for even attempting to freeze it  it became so hot that the research staff  had to leave the room an attending  doctor's pen melted the plastic burning  his hands steam rose off the sides of  its body fogging up the windows of the  room the test was abandoned after the  size of the containment chamber began to  melt and they worried the creature would  be able to breach containment once it  was left alone 682 cooled back down to  its usual temperature maybe we should  see what happens if we try a slightly  greener method of destruction 682 was  exposed to scp-166  a young nature spirit that can cause  organic matter in her vicinity to  decompose as soon as 166 was released  into its chamber 682 began to run toward  her even as its body began to melt as it  got closer it began to decay and fall  apart more rapidly pieces of its body  softening and slothing off in chunks by  the time it reached 166 it had melted  down into the shape of a patch of grass  covered with colorful wildflowers 15  minutes later it began to regenerate  itself as it usually does its body  reconstituting at the same rate it was  melting the regeneration process began  to speed up going faster and faster  until it surpassed the rate of melting a  piece of the monster would soften and  flop to the ground but by the time it  landed a patch of regrowth had already  replaced it it eventually beat the  melting process and regenerated to its  original form with one difference it had  a sprinkling of flowers and mushrooms on  its back resembling a forest clearing it  was almost pretty even on top of such a  foul creature until a full-sized tree  suddenly burst out of its back shooting  up to a height of 10 feet and puncturing  the roof of its containment chamber and  i'm afraid that's all we have time for  for one video but this only just  scratches the surface of the weird and  wild mutations we've come to expect from  scp-682 want another video on even more  crazy mutations from the hard to destroy  reptile make your feelings known down in  the comments now go check out how to  kill  scp-682 theories and ideas and  scp-682 waze scp foundation tried to  kill hard to destroy reptile for more  about the foundation's face-offs with  this seemingly indestructible beast
 

